{"message":{"content":[{"text":"Report this durable work update to the CEO in your normal voice. State the outcome and any material limitations in concise plain language. Do not name internal components, validation checks or technical failure details. Never claim work started or finished without the supplied evidence. Do not ask for routine retry or implementation decisions. Only an explicitly supplied CEO decision requires an answer. Host evidence:\nFinished and checked: CEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\n\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\n\nEvidence: [TaskProgress { state: Passed, attempts: 1, evidence: [\"Independently verify the complete deliverable and every acceptance constraint in this verbatim contract. Preserve prohibitions. Do not certify partial completion.\\nCEO request (verbatim):\\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\\n\\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\\n: Inspected the company working area directly (/private/var/folders/mx/w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn/T/richos-owned-desktop-v2fhgxxv/company).\\n\\n1) File exists: Read of company/hello.txt returns a single line, `Hello Rich`.\\n\\n2) Exact byte content, no trailing newline (byte-level check, not eyeballing): ripgrep in multiline mode with pattern `\\\\A\\\\x48\\\\x65\\\\x6c\\\\x6c\\\\x6f\\\\x20\\\\x52\\\\x69\\\\x63\\\\x68\\\\z` matched 1 occurrence in hello.txt. Anchoring \\\\A...\\\\z around the explicit byte sequence 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 52 69 63 68 proves the file's entire contents are exactly the 10 bytes `Hello Rich` — correct capitalization, single space, no BOM, no leading/trailing whitespace, and nothing after the final `h`.\\n\\n3) Trailing-newline negative checks (two independent confirmations): `\\\\n` in multiline mode -> 0 occurrences across 0 files (no newline byte anywhere in the file); `Rich.` with multiline-dotall (dot matches newline) -> 0 occurrences, so no character of any kind follows `Rich`.\\n\\n4) No other files created: Glob `**/*` in the company directory returns exactly one path, `hello.txt`. Glob `**/.*` returns no files, so there are no hidden scratch files, backups, .bak/.tmp/.orig artifacts, or accompanying notes. Nothing else exists in the working area, so nothing could have been overwritten or removed to make room for the deliverable, and no notes/README were added alongside it.\\n\\nAll acceptance constraints in the verbatim contract are satisfied: hello.txt in the company working area, contents exactly `Hello Rich`, no trailing newline, no other characters before or after, and no other files created.\\n\\nSeparately, and not a condition of this deliverable: Rich's offer to run a ~20-minute intake on what the company does, who it's for, and how the CEO wants Rich to work — and to write those answers into a durable record — remains outstanding. Rich stated it can wait until this task is off the CEO's desk; that condition is now met, so it is available to schedule at the CEO's convenience.\"], retry_at: 1788939406554, review_pending: false, review_failures: 0, recovery_cycles: 2 }]","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"type":"user"}
